# Wave W17-O (Ragged Pass): stair turf — ledge grass on the mountain’s broken stair: warm grass worn thin at the ledge lips, pale stone-dust flecks where a thousand knees and boots have scuffed the edges (design: calm speckled grass on a broken ledged stair down a mountainside, warm earthy palette). The Pass’s own ground — warmer and more olive than Route 112’s ash-flecked slope grass, and split from it by the worn-lip register: this grass is STAIR-worn, not ash-dusted.
